  "confirmed_observations": [
    "All 19 Adapter tensors changed and remained finite per real training audit. Change alone does not prove learned content sensitivity because AdamW decay can change a parameter with zero-valued gradients; nonzero optimizer moments and layer responses must be examined separately.",
    "The trained MLP and attention use small input scales, ordinary Linear biases, and no per-vector Q/K normalization or learned temperature.",
    "Final trained parameter/moment and actual-dev numerical statistics are reported directly; no random surrogate is claimed to be actual initialization."
  ],
  "conditional_interpretation": [
    "If final affine outputs show a much larger dataset-common mean than centered residual, near-parallel value projections have a present-state common-component explanation. Direct bias and projected common input may both contribute; norms of correlated components are not additive causal shares.",
    "If within-neighbor logits are tiny and float64 attention is near uniform, that is a measured numerical scale issue; sqrt(head_dim) is the standard operation and not by itself a bug.",
    "Gate acts after attention and cannot create uniform attention weights.",
    "Small query/key gradients can follow from near-identical values: redistributing attention then changes output little. Uniform softmax has nonzero derivatives, so entropy near one alone does not prove a zero-gradient bug.",
    "Learning rate, initialization, loss incentives, input geometry and Adam epsilon may interact. This audit cannot identify a unique historical cause or justify simply increasing lr.",
    "Adding a common bias to every K_j changes each query logit by the same constant Q·bias/sqrt(d), which softmax cancels exactly. A shared V offset survives as a common output component. Therefore value-bias domination and near-uniform logits are distinct mechanisms, not one direct cause.",
    "Adding the same b2 to normal/random value means leaves their pre-MHA absolute difference unchanged but can increase their shared norm and cosine. This is relative contrast dilution, not proof of destroyed absolute information.",
    "The final Q/query moment data-to-decay ratios quantify the current weak optimization signal; they do not reconstruct historical steps or identify a unique learning-rate cause."
  ],
